What was changed
----------------
Rebranding only: product name, binary and package names, wordmark and
installer artwork, documentation, distribution channels (npm, Homebrew, Scoop,
install scripts) and the automated upstream synchronization workflow. The
application source is derived from the upstream project, and the upstream
copyright notices in LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE apply unchanged to the
derived portions.

Preserved from upstream
-----------------------
The "moviebox" content provider module (src/providers/moviebox/), its wire
protocol, provider identity and configuration key (moviebox_enabled) are
upstream compatibility interfaces and are deliberately not renamed. Third-party
dependencies keep their own licences.

